# Frontend Performance

## Eliminating Waterfalls (CRITICAL)
- Check cheap sync conditions before awaiting remote values
- Move `await` into branches where actually used — don't block early
- Use `Promise.all()` for independent async operations
- Start promises early, await late
- Use Suspense boundaries to stream content progressively

```tsx
// ❌ Sequential (waterfall)
const user = await getUser(id);
const orders = await getOrders(id);

// ✅ Parallel
const [user, orders] = await Promise.all([getUser(id), getOrders(id)]);
```

## Bundle Size Optimization (CRITICAL)
- **No barrel imports** — import directly from the module file, not `index.ts`
- **Dynamic imports** for heavy components not needed on initial load
- **Defer third-party scripts** (analytics, logging) — load after hydration
- **Conditional loading** — load modules only when feature is activated
- **Preload on hover/focus** for perceived speed on navigation

```tsx
// ❌ Barrel import pulls entire library
import { Button, Dialog, Tooltip } from '@/components';

// ✅ Direct imports — tree-shakeable
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { Dialog } from '@/components/ui/dialog';

// ✅ Dynamic import for heavy component
const HeavyChart = lazy(() => import('@/components/charts/HeavyChart'));
```

For full detail, read `.kiro/steering/rerender-optimization.md`.

# Frontend Testing Patterns

## Testing Levels

| Level | Tool | % of Tests | Description |
|-------|------|-----------|-------------|
| 1 | Vitest + React Testing Library | 60% | Component tests — render, interact, assert |
| 2 | Vitest + MSW | 25% | Integration — components with API calls |
| 3 | Playwright | 15% | E2E — full user flows in real browser |

**Default: Level 1 (component tests) unless told otherwise.**

## Test File Structure
```
src/views/{module}/
├── components/
│   └── BookingCard.tsx
└── __tests__/
    └── BookingCard.test.tsx

e2e/
├── login.spec.ts
└── fixtures/
    └── auth.ts
```

## Key Rules
- Locator priority: `getByRole` > `getByLabel` > `getByText` > `data-testid`
- Mock APIs at network level (MSW), never at hook level
- Test behavior and user interactions, not implementation details
- Every component needs: happy path, loading, error, and empty state tests
- Use `userEvent` over `fireEvent` for realistic interactions
- Wrap state updates in `act()` or use `waitFor()`

## Component Test Pattern
```tsx
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';
import { BookingCard } from '../components/BookingCard';

describe('BookingCard', () => {
  it('renders booking details', () => {
    render(<BookingCard booking={mockBooking} />);
    expect(screen.getByRole('heading', { name: /booking/i })).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('calls onCancel when cancel button clicked', async () => {
    const onCancel = vi.fn();
    render(<BookingCard booking={mockBooking} onCancel={onCancel} />);
    await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /cancel/i }));
    expect(onCancel).toHaveBeenCalledWith(mockBooking.id);
  });
});
```

## MSW API Mocking Pattern
```tsx
import { http, HttpResponse } from 'msw';
import { setupServer } from 'msw/node';

const server = setupServer(
  http.get('/api/bookings', () => HttpResponse.json({ items: [mockBooking] }))
);

beforeAll(() => server.listen());
afterEach(() => server.resetHandlers());
afterAll(() => server.close());
```

For full detail, read `.kiro/steering/testing/FRONTEND_TESTING_STEERING.md`.

